# AI usage — session hygiene

## Sessions

- **One task ≈ one chat.** New feature or doc pass → new session (`/clear`).
- Do **not** continue multi-day threads. Long context (>150k) is expensive.
- Prefer `/clear` when switching goals.

## Models

| Work | Prefer |
| ---- | ------ |
| Implementation, UI port, docs | **Composer** (Cursor) / Sonnet (Claude) |
| Hard architecture, money-math bugs | Sonnet + thinking (sparingly) |
| Opus / Max Mode | Rare — explicit hard judgment only |

Do **not** use high-thinking for spacing, copy tweaks, or mechanical ports.

## Subagents

- Default: **no subagents.** One agent + targeted `rg`/`Read`.
- Spawn explore/verify only when the user asks or scope truly requires it.

## MCP

- **neon** (OAuth), **context7**, **playwright**, **markitdown** — use when relevant.
- Skip failed/unauth servers; do not retry auth loops.
- Prefer `rg` / `Read` over Playwright for code questions.

## Cross-session context

- **`docs/PROJECT.md`**, **`docs/workflow/in-progress/sveltekit-migration.md`**, route guides — then `/clear` between tasks.

## Dual repo sessions

If **kame-homes** is also open, ignore its Supabase/Next.js-specific rules for kame-lends work.
